// Annex B: "Keywords are predefined nonescaped identifiers that define
// Verilog-AMS language constructs. [...] Verilog-AMS reserves the keywords
// listed in Table B.1." `if` is in Table B.1, so the spelling is not available
// as an ordinary identifier.
//
// This file pins the reservation at the VARIABLE-NAME position: a real
// declaration's list of identifiers (A.2.1.3) bottoms out in `identifier`, which
// §2.8 defines to exclude the keywords. Same rule as
// 03_reserved_module_rejected.va, different grammar position — a compiler that
// special-cased only the module header would pass that one and fail this.
//
// The reject pins the diagnostic CODE, not the prose: `identifier` — what this
// file used to demand — is a fragment of the diagnostic's title, so rewording
// the catalogue entry would silently stop this fixture proving anything.
//
// So is `if` itself: E0208's title is "identIFier", and a `//! reject` pattern is
// matched against the catalogue title as well as against the message
// (tests/torture.zig failureContains). The `//! reject if` line below therefore
// discriminates nothing on its own; it is kept because the chapter counts
// covered spellings by their reject lines (14_include_reserved.va). The proof is
// that this file declares exactly ONE thing, so the E0208 can only have come
// from `real if;`. 24_reserved_exp.va and 25_reserved_or.va exist for the same
// reason.
//! lrm B
//! lrm 2.8
//! lrm 2.8.2
//! reject E0208
//! reject if
module annex_b_reserved_if_rejected;
    real if;
endmodule
